From 551a1c2d1c6728c1974c4d1d1f71e640d8120174 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "David J. Shepard II" <daveman1010220@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:06:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(vigild): the reaper no longer loses a service's exit
 status

As PID 1 (or with --reaper), vigild's reaper drains every exited child
with waitpid(-1, WNOHANG) on each SIGCHLD. That collects vigild's own
children too, services and exec checks, which tokio waits on: a pidfd
tells tokio its child exited, but does not stop another waitpid from
collecting it first. When the reaper won, tokio's wait failed with
ECHILD and the exit status was lost: a service that exited 0 was
reported as `success=false exit_code=1` and handled by its on-failure
policy (restarted, or failure-shutdown with exit code 10), and an exec
check that passed counted as failed.

Seen on a container whose one-shot service runs right as other services
start: it exited 0 and was reported failed on two of three starts.

The reaper now keeps each status it collects, for 60 s, and
reaper::wait_child, which the service actor and the exec probe use in
place of Child::wait, takes it from there when the wait fails with
ECHILD.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAe3biqjeQJRMfngB95eyW
